"""Town and region data for the locations/mortgage-broker-{town}.html pages.

Facts only. Every local note, FAQ and tag detail below is either general NZ
lending practice or a verifiable local fact (council, geography, industry,
named events with their year). No rates, prices, populations, distances we
haven't checked, or claims about Finch's own client history.

Tags drive the shared lending-factor copy in generate_town_pages.py; their
values carry the town-specific detail so no two pages read the same. Tag order
is priority order: the first tags become the page's headline local points.

Coordinates come from OpenStreetMap Nominatim (October 2026).
"""


def T(slug, name, region, council, hub, near, tags, note, faqs, district=None, prose=None):
    # district: label for the hero eyebrow when the council name doesn't fit.
    # prose: how the place reads mid-sentence ("in the Chatham Islands").
    return {"slug": slug, "name": name, "region": region, "council": council,
            "hub": hub, "near": near, "tags": tags, "note": note, "faqs": faqs,
            "district": district, "prose": prose or name}


